ps, each having its strengths and weaknesses, to complete various space missions.\n\n5. Missions and quests: The player can accept missions from the inhabitants of the planets they visit, which may involve combat, diplomacy, infiltration, or exploration. Completing these quests will reward the player with experience points, resources, or items.\n\n6. Trading and diplomacy: The player can interact with various factions and alien races, where they can establish alliances, trade for resources, or negotiate treaties. The player's standing with each faction is affected by their actions and will have consequences in the game world.\n\n7. Space combat: The player will face various pirates, hostile alien creatures, and enemy fleets during their journey. The combat will involve real-time tactical decision-making, with each spaceship having its unique abilities and attack patterns.\n\nMultiplayer:\n\n1. Online co-op mode: Cosmic Quest will have an online co-op mode, allowing players to team up with friends and explore the galaxy together, share resources, and complete challenging quests.\n\n2. Player vs. Player (PvP) mode: Players can engage in PvP battles against each other to test their fleet's strength and strategy. They can also obtain rare resources and items by winning these battles.\n\n3. Leaderboards and achievements: Players can earn achievements and climb the leaderboards, competing against other players and showcasing their mastery of the game.\n\nMonetization:\n\n1. Cosmic Quest will have an initial purchase price.\n\n2. Downloadable content (DLC) packs will be available for players to purchase, adding new content such as planets, missions, spaceships, and cosmetic items.\n\n3. Optional in-game cosmetics, like character skins and spaceship design elements, can be purchased with real money. These items will not affect gameplay or give an unfair advantage.", "country": null, "hashed_ip": null, "header": null, "language": "English", "redacted": false, "role": "assist