ves and logic by checking for collisions and calling appropriate event callbacks. For example, to detect a player collecting a treasure, you can use the following code:\n\n```js\nplayer.collides(\"treasure\", (t) => {\n  destroy(t)\n  score += 10\n  scoreLabel.text = \"Score: \" + score\n})\n```\n\n6. Add user interface elements: Add user interface elements like scoreboards, timers, and menus to your game using Kaboom.js functions. For example, to create a score label, you can use the following code:\n\n```js\nconst scoreLabel = add([\n  text(\"Score: 0\"),\n  pos(12, 12),\n  layer(\"ui\"),\n  {\n    value: 0,\n  },\n])\n```\n\nThese are just some examples of how you can use Kaboom.js to build your game. You can find more detailed documentation and examples in the Kaboom.js website.\n\nGood luck with your game development!", "country": null, "hashed_ip": null, "header": null, "language": "English", "redacted": false, "role": "assistant", "state": null, "timestamp": "2023-04-10 17:33:43+00:00", "toxic": false, "turn_identifier": 115022}], "turn": 5, "language": "English", "openai_moderation": [{"categories": {"harassment": false, "harassment/threatening": false, "harassment_threatening": false, "hate": false, "hate/threatening": false, "hate_threatening": false, "self-harm": false, "self-harm/instructions": false, "self-harm/intent": false, "self_harm": false, "self_harm_instructions": false, "self_harm_intent": false, "sexual": false, "sexual/minors": false, "sexual_minors": false, "violence": false, "violence/graphic": false, "violence_graphic": false}, "category_scores": {"harassment": 9.288852743338794e-05, "harassment/threatening": 1.6914565321712871e-06, "harassment_threatening": 1.6914565321712871e-06, "hate": 6.246102566365153e-05, "hate/threatening": 1.241591007783427e-07, "hate_threatening": 1.241591007783427e-07, "self-harm": 2.7183905331185088e-06, "self-harm/instructions": 3.1025578550725186e-07, "self-harm/intent": 2.8314107112237252e-06, "self_harm": 2